From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:23:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] perf(previews): versioned previews are immutable and
 their versions outlive a restart

The editor's culled frames show /i/<id>.jpg?preview&v=<updatedAt>, hundreds
a page.

- A response for the frame's current version is 'immutable' for a year, so
  a page of previews costs no request on the next visit (was max-age=60,
  no validator).
- The version a thumbnail was rendered from is stored beside it
  (thumb/<id>.ver) and read back once per frame after a restart. Without
  it a restart forgot every version and re-rendered each previewed frame.
- A request for the current version, when the stored thumbnail is on
  record as older, waits for the render (deduped, capped, metered) instead
  of pinning the old picture on a frame that shows it until its next edit.
  A thumbnail of unknown age (stored before versions were) is still served
  at once and refreshed in the background.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
